<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's CCE in deal to make Aiwa stereos.</title>
<headline>Brazil's CCE in deal to make Aiwa stereos.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian eletronics firm CCE said it has struck an agreement with Japanese electronic good maker Aiwa Co Ltd to produce Aiwa stereos in Brazil and sell them in four-nation Mercosur customs union.</p>
<p>The two firms together so far have invested $30 million in the deal and CCE expects to begin output of Aiwa stereo minisystems in 1997, a CCE spokesman said.</p>
<p>Aiwa and CCE executives will hold a press conference on Nov 26 at 1100 local/1300 gmt to give details about the partnership.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415.</p>
